Article 69

The Regional Government, in order to provide protection to children:

a. prevent violence against children by optimizing the role of customary institutions;
b. conduct socialization, seminars and outreach on child protection and rights;
c. develop child-friendly school models;
d. provide public facilities that are friendly and safe for children;
e. compile databases and information on acts of violence against children; f. map locations and areas prone to violence against children;
g. coordinate and cooperate in preventing violations of children's rights;
h. strengthen the function of institutions or organizations engaged in child protection; and
i. encourage public awareness of the importance of child protection by establishing women and child protection assistants.

The service efforts undertaken by the Regional Government towards women victims of violence as referred to in Article 20 through Article 33 shall apply mutatis mutandis to service efforts for women victims of violence.

